.TH THERMO 1 "2026-05-09" "thermoservice 0.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thermo \- read DS18B20 temperature sensor and print result to stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thermo
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B thermo
reads the current temperature from the first DS18B20 1-Wire temperature sensor
found under
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/28*
and prints the value in degrees Celsius to standard output, formatted to three
decimal places.
.PP
If no sensor is detected, the program prints a diagnostic message and exits
with status 0.
.SH OUTPUT
A single line of the form:
.PP
.RS
.I 23.125
.RE
.PP
representing the temperature in degrees Celsius.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/28*/w1_slave
Kernel 1-Wire sysfs interface for DS18B20 sensors.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including when no sensor is detected).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thermoservice (8),
.BR ha_push (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>
